msgid "she"
msgstr "彼女"

#. [ES10-0112] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2 Interceptor] | Text role: substitution <enemy> | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Inserted fragment; review grammar in parent sentence. Key <enemy> remains unchanged. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:862
msgctxt "ES10-0112"
msgid "Hammer"
msgstr "ハンマー"

#. [ES10-0113] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2 Interceptor] | Text role: substitution <magnitude> | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Inserted fragment; review grammar in parent sentence. Key <magnitude> remains unchanged. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:863
msgctxt "ES10-0113"
msgid "ten"
msgstr "10"

#. [ES10-0114] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2.1 Interceptor] | Text role: name | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <system> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:876
msgctxt "ES10-0114"
msgid "Mine asteroids in {1}"
msgstr "{1}で小惑星を採掘せよ"

#. [ES10-0115] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2.1 Interceptor] | Text role: description | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <system>; <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:877
msgctxt "ES10-0115"
msgid "Go to the {1} system and mine five tons of silicon, then land on {2}."
msgstr "{1}星系へ向かい、シリコンを5トン採掘し、{2}に着陸せよ。"

#. [ES10-0116] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2.1 Interceptor] | Text role: blocked | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first>; <capacity> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:878
msgctxt "ES10-0116"
msgid "When you meet up with James in the spaceport, he says, \"Hi there, {1}! I think you'll find what I want to show you next very interesting, but you'll need to free up {2} first. So, you'll either have to cancel another mission, or come back here later to continue this one. Sorry!\""
msgstr "宇宙港でジェームズと落ち合うと、彼は言う。「やあ、{1}！次に君に見せたいものにはきっと興味を持ってくれると思うが、その前に{2}を空ける必要がある。だから、別のミッションをキャンセルするか、後でまたここに戻ってきてこのミッションを続けるか、どちらかにしてくれ。すまない！」"

#. [ES10-0117] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2.1 Interceptor] | Text role: substitution <captain> | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Inserted fragment; review grammar in parent sentence. Key <captain> remains unchanged. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:886
msgctxt "ES10-0117"
msgid "Marshall"
msgstr "マーシャル"

#. [ES10-0118] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2.1 Interceptor] | Text role: substitution <they> | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Inserted fragment; review grammar in parent sentence. Key <they> remains unchanged. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:887
msgctxt "ES10-0118"
msgid "he"
msgstr "彼"

#. [ES10-0119] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2.1 Interceptor] | Text role: dialog | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <destination> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:893
msgctxt "ES10-0119"
msgid "You've reached {1}, but you don't have at least five tons of silicon in your cargo hold. Locate and mine silicon asteroids in this system before returning."
msgstr "{1}に到着しましたが、貨物室にシリコンが5トン以上ありません。この星系内でシリコンを含む小惑星を見つけて採掘してから戻ってきてください。"

#. [ES10-0120] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [2.1 Interceptor] | Text role: mission cargo name | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Translate display only; retain canonical cargo key. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:896
msgctxt "ES10-0120"
msgid "Silicon"
msgstr "シリコン"

#. [ES10-0124] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [3 Interceptor] | Text role: log | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:917
msgctxt "ES10-0124"
msgid "Dropped James off on Hestia after running a few missions with him. Escort duty is a risky business."
msgstr "ジェームズといくつかのミッションをこなした後、ヘスティアで彼を降ろした。護衛任務は危険な仕事だ。"

#. [ES10-0128] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:23
msgctxt "ES10-0128"
msgid "With some trepidation, you give the shipyard owner your money and take your new ship for a test drive, piloting it out of the shipyard and onto a spare landing pad by the spaceport. Then you get out and look the ship over a bit more closely. You are busy polishing out a few rust spots with a piece of steel wool when an old man in grease-stained coveralls walks up."
msgstr "多少の不安を感じながらも、あなたは造船所のオーナーに金を払い、新しい船を試運転する。造船所から船を操縦して、宇宙港のそばの空いている着陸パッドへ向かう。それから船を降りて、もう少しじっくりと船を見てみる。スチールウールで錆びた箇所をいくつか磨き落としていると、油汚れのついたつなぎを着た老人が歩み寄ってくる。"

#. [ES10-0129] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:24
msgctxt "ES10-0129"
msgid "{1}\"Nothing quite like buying your very first starship,\" he says."
msgstr "{1}「初めて自分の宇宙船を買うというのは、何物にも代えがたいものだね」と彼は言う。"

#. [ES10-0130] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:26
msgctxt "ES10-0130"
msgid "{1}\"Yeah, I'm still kind of in shock over how much money I spent.\""
msgstr "{1}「ええ、使った金額の大きさに、まだちょっとショックを受けているんです。」"

#. [ES10-0131] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:28
msgctxt "ES10-0131"
msgid "{1}\"Well, I don't plan to get too attached to this one. I'll be flying something much nicer before long.\""
msgstr "{1}「まあ、この船にあまり愛着を持つつもりはないよ。すぐに、もっといい船に乗るつもりだからね。」"

#. [ES10-0132] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:30
msgctxt "ES10-0132"
msgid "{1}\"Beat it, old-timer, I've got more important things to do than chat with you.\""
msgstr "{1}「失せな、じいさん。あんたとおしゃべりするより大事な用があるんだ。」"

#. [ES10-0133] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:33
msgctxt "ES10-0133"
msgid "{1}He grins. \"I know the feeling. It's a crime how much interest the banks charge to first-timers. It's been that way ever since when I first started out.\""
msgstr "{1}彼はにやりと笑う。「その気持ちはよくわかるよ。初めて船を買う人に銀行がふっかける利息は犯罪的だ。私が船に乗り始めた頃からずっとそうだったよ。」"

#. [ES10-0134] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:36
msgctxt "ES10-0134"
msgid "{1}He smiles. \"I'm sure you will. But there's something nice to having a ship you can pilot all by yourself. Believe me, once you have to start managing crew and paying salaries, or keeping track of a whole fleet, you'll miss these days when everything was simple.\""
msgstr "{1}彼は微笑む。「君ならきっとそうなるだろうね。だが、自分一人で操縦できる船というのも悪くないものだ。信じてくれ、乗組員を管理して給料を払ったり、船団全体を把握したりするようになると、すべてが単純だったこの頃が恋しくなるはずだ。」"

#. [ES10-0135] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:91
msgctxt "ES10-0135"
msgid "{1}\"You're a captain?\" you ask."
msgstr "{1}「あなたは船長なんですか？」とあなたは尋ねる。"

#. [ES10-0136] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:92
msgctxt "ES10-0136"
msgid "{1}\"Was,\" he says. \"Sold off my fleet a few days ago, and I already miss it. But it was time. Time for me to retire.\" His voice trails off, then his face lights up. \"Say, any chance I could hitch a ride with you, maybe show you the ropes, give you some pointers? I could pay you, of course.\""
msgstr "{1}「そうだった」と彼は言う。「数日前に船団をすべて売却したばかりで、もう恋しいよ。だが、潮時だったんだ。引退する時が来たのさ。」彼の声は小さくなり、やがて顔が明るくなった。「なあ、君の船に乗せてもらえないか？いろいろ教えたり、助言したりできるかもしれない。もちろん、乗せてもらう分の金は払うよ。」"

#. [ES10-0137] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:94
msgctxt "ES10-0137"
msgid "{1}\"Sure, where are you trying to get to?\""
msgstr "{1}「いいですよ、どこへ行きたいのですか？」"

#. [ES10-0138] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:95
msgctxt "ES10-0138"
msgid "{1}\"I'd rather figure things out on my own.\""
msgstr "{1}「自分で何とかしたいので。」"

#. [ES10-0139] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:97
msgctxt "ES10-0139"
msgid "{1}\"Well,\" he says, \"I've got a spot reserved in a retirement home, but I don't mind taking a roundabout way to get there. For starters, how about you give me a lift to {2}? It's just one jump away from here; I can mark it on your map.\""
msgstr "{1}「そうだな」と彼は言う。「老人ホームに入居枠は確保してあるが、そこへ行くまで遠回りしても構わない。まずは、{2}まで送ってくれないか？ここから1回ジャンプするだけだ。君の地図に印を付けておこう。」"

#. [ES10-0140] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:99
msgctxt "ES10-0140"
msgid "{1}\"Sounds good!\""
msgstr "{1}「いいですね！」"

#. [ES10-0141] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:101
msgctxt "ES10-0141"
msgid "{1}\"How much will you pay me?\""
msgstr "{1}「いくら払ってくれるんですか？」"

#. [ES10-0142] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:102
msgctxt "ES10-0142"
msgid "{1}\"That's kind of a rude question,\" he says, \"but I'll pay you ten thousand credits. I guarantee you that's more than any captain ever gets for carrying one passenger for one day.\""
msgstr "{1}「ちょっと失礼な質問だね」と彼は言う。「だが、1万クレジット払おう。乗客1人を1日乗せる報酬としては、どんな船長が受け取る額よりも多いと保証するよ。」"

#. [ES10-0143] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:104
msgctxt "ES10-0143"
msgid "{1}\"That's really generous. Thank you.\""
msgstr "{1}「本当に寛大ですね。ありがとうございます。」"

#. [ES10-0144] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:106
msgctxt "ES10-0144"
msgid "{1}\"You're treating me like a charity case? No thanks, I'll earn my money legitimately.\""
msgstr "{1}「私を施しが必要な人間だと思っているんですか？結構です。お金は自分でまっとうに稼ぎます。」"

#. [ES10-0145] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:109
msgctxt "ES10-0145"
msgid "{1}\"Great,\" he says. \"My name is James, by the way.\""
msgstr "{1}「よかった」と彼は言う。「そういえば、私の名前はジェームズだ。」"

#. [ES10-0146] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first>; <last> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:110
msgctxt "ES10-0146"
msgid "{1}\"{2} {3},\" you say."
msgstr "{1}「{2} {3}です」とあなたは言う。"

#. [ES10-0147] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <last> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:111
msgctxt "ES10-0147"
msgid "{1}\"I'm looking forward to traveling with you, Captain {2},\" says James."
msgstr "{1}「君と旅ができるのを楽しみにしているよ、{2}船長」とジェームズは言う。"

#. [ES10-0148] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first>; <last> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:114
msgctxt "ES10-0148"
msgid "{1}\"{2} {3}?\" he stops for a moment. \"I've heard that name before. Reminds me of someone famous, I think,\" says James. \"Anyways, I'm looking forward to traveling with you.\""
msgstr "{1}「{2} {3}？」彼は一瞬言葉を切る。「その名前、聞いたことがあるな。たしか、誰か有名人を思い出す名前だ」とジェームズは言う。「とにかく、君と旅ができるのを楽しみにしているよ」"

#. [ES10-0149] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <trade>; <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:118
msgctxt "ES10-0149"
msgid "{1}As you're helping him wheel his luggage aboard and showing him his bunk, he says, \"Before we take off, you might head on over to the trading center and {2}; we can sell those for a good profit on {3}."
msgstr "{1}彼が荷物を船内に運び込むのを手伝い、寝台を案内していると、彼は言う。「出発する前に、交易センターへ行って{2}を仕入れるといい。{3}なら高く売れるはずだ」"

#. [ES10-0150] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro mission" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <while> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:119
msgctxt "ES10-0150"
msgid "{1}\"Also make sure to visit the local outfitter. {2}, every world with an outfitter will at least carry a map with information on the neighboring systems. Buying them can help if you're not quite sure where you're going.\""
msgstr "{1}「それから、地元の装備屋にも必ず寄るように。{2}、装備屋がある世界ならどこでも、少なくとも近隣星系の情報が載った地図は売っているはずだ。行き先がはっきりしないなら、買っておくと役に立つよ」"

#. [ES10-0151] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mission intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:124
msgctxt "ES10-0151"
msgid "As you land on {1}, James says, \"Congrats on your first trip through hyperspace! I'm impressed that you didn't throw up; most folks do, the first time.\""
msgstr "{1}に着陸すると、ジェームズは言う。「初めてのハイパースペース航行、おめでとう！吐かなかったなんて感心したよ。たいていの人は初回は吐いてしまうからね」"

#. [ES10-0152] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mission intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:125
msgctxt "ES10-0152"
msgid "{1}\"Including you?\" you ask."
msgstr "{1}「あなたもですか？」とあなたは尋ねる。"

#. [ES10-0153] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mission intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <payment> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:126
msgctxt "ES10-0153"
msgid "{1}\"Yeah, and then spent half an hour in orbit cleaning my cabin while hoping the passengers wouldn't come out of their bunk room and see the mess. Not my proudest moment. Anyway, here's your pay.\" He hands you {2}."
msgstr "{1}「ああ。その後、軌道上で30分かけて船室を掃除したよ。乗客が寝室から出てきて惨状を見ないことを祈りながらね。誇れる瞬間じゃなかったよ。とにかく、これが報酬だ」彼はあなたに{2}を手渡す。"

#. [ES10-0154] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mission intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:127
msgctxt "ES10-0154"
msgid "{1}Then he adds, \"If you're okay with giving me a lift for a while longer, sell off any of that cargo you bought and then meet me in the spaceport. I'll see if I can rustle up any interesting work for you to do.\""
msgstr "{1}そして彼は付け加える。「もしよければ、もう少しの間乗せてくれないか。買った貨物を売ってから、宇宙港で会おう。何か面白い仕事がないか探してみるよ」"

#. [ES10-0155] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mission intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: All classic routes (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:129
msgctxt "ES10-0155"
msgid "{1}(Click the \"Spaceport\" button to continue this mission.)"
msgstr "{1}（このミッションを続けるには「宇宙港」ボタンをクリックしてください）"

#. [ES10-0156] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro earth offer" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <origin> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:134
msgctxt "ES10-0156"
msgid "The spaceport on {1} is so big and crowded that it takes a long time to find James. The sheer number of people here is almost overwhelming. Homeless men wrapped in old army blankets beg money from well-dressed businessmen. Soldiers in Navy uniforms walk by in groups of ten or twenty, all marching in unison. Starship captains haggle with merchants over trade goods and jobs. Flashes of light come from various landing bays as welders make repairs."
msgstr "{1}の宇宙港は非常に大きく混雑しており、ジェームズを見つけるのに時間がかかる。ここにいる人の多さは圧倒的だ。古い軍用毛布にくるまったホームレスの男たちが、身なりのいいビジネスマンに金をせびっている。海軍の制服を着た兵士たちが10人、20人ほどの集団で足並みをそろえて行進していく。宇宙船の船長たちは商人たちと交易品や仕事の条件について交渉している。さまざまな着陸ベイでは、溶接工が修理を行うたびに光がちらつく。"

#. [ES10-0157] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro earth offer" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <they've> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:135
msgctxt "ES10-0157"
msgid "{1}When you find James, he's standing by a window, looking out at the city, watching the starships taking off and landing in a continuous stream. \"This is it,\" he says, \"where our race began. The world that all the tourists want to visit, and that no one wants to live on. Twenty billion people, more industry and exports than any other place in the galaxy. But underneath it all, poverty of a completely different sort from what {2} got in the Dirt Belt.\""
msgstr "{1}ジェームズを見つけると、彼は窓際に立ち、外の街を眺めながら、絶え間なく離着陸する宇宙船を見ていた。「ここがそうだよ」と彼は言う。「我々の種族が生まれた場所だ。観光客は皆訪れたがるが、誰も住みたがらない世界。200億の人口を抱え、銀河のどの場所よりも産業と輸出が盛んだ。だがその裏には、{2}がダートベルトで経験したのとは全く別の種類の貧困があるんだ」"

#. [ES10-0158] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro earth offer" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <destination> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:136
msgctxt "ES10-0158"
msgid "{1}After taking one last glance out the window, he says, \"Anyway, we're nearing my destination. Are you willing to take me on one last trip? I need to get to {2}, and of course I'll pay you quite well to take me there.\""
msgstr "{1}窓の外を最後に一瞥してから、彼は言う。「とにかく、目的地が近づいてきた。最後にもう一度だけ、私を乗せていってくれないか？{2}に行く必要があるんだ。もちろん、そこまで乗せていってくれれば十分な報酬を払うよ」"

#. [ES10-0159] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro earth offer" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. [ES10-0301] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:455
msgctxt "ES10-0159"
msgid "{1}\"Of course.\""
msgstr "{1}「もちろんです」"

#. [ES10-0160] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro earth offer" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:139
msgctxt "ES10-0160"
msgid "{1}\"Sorry, but I was planning on heading out in a different direction from here.\""
msgstr "{1}「すみませんが、ここからは別の方向へ向かう予定なんです」"

#. [ES10-0161] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro earth offer" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. [ES10-0204] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro ingot" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. [ES10-0303] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:458
msgctxt "ES10-0161"
msgid "{1}Once again you walk back to your ship with James. Once you get there, as he's stowing his luggage, you pull up the information your computer has on {2}. It's one of the \"Paradise Worlds,\" terraformed to have a perfect climate, accessible only to the very wealthy. You wonder whether James is going to be able to fit in there."
msgstr "{1}再びジェームズと共に船へ戻る。船に着き、彼が荷物を積み込んでいる間に、あなたはコンピュータで{2}に関する情報を引き出す。そこは「パラダイス・ワールド」の一つで、完璧な気候になるようテラフォーミングされており、富裕層しか立ち入れない場所だ。あなたはジェームズがそこに馴染めるのか疑問に思う。"

#. [ES10-0162] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro earth offer" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:146
msgctxt "ES10-0162"
msgid "{1}Once again you walk back to your ship with James. You've heard of {2} before; one of the Paradise Worlds terraformed from a lifeless ice planet to the largest and most luxurious retirement home in the galaxy. As you look at his utilitarian outfit and modest luggage, something seems off about the idea of James living in such a place."
msgstr "{1}再びあなたはジェームズと共に船へ戻る。あなたは以前に{2}について聞いたことがある。生命のいない氷の惑星をテラフォームして造られた、銀河最大かつ最も豪華な老人ホームであるパラダイス・ワールドの一つだ。彼の質素な服装と控えめな荷物を見ると、ジェームズがそのような場所に住むという考えには何か違和感がある。"

#. [ES10-0163] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet>; <intro end suit> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2253
msgctxt "ES10-0163"
msgid "As you are piloting your ship down to land on {1}, James disappears into his bunk room. After the ship has landed he comes out, no longer in the grease-stained coveralls he's been wearing up until now, but in a suit.{2} He smooths down the front of the suit distractedly and then looks at his hands as if unsure of where to put them. \"How do I look?\" he asks."
msgstr "あなたが船を操縦して{1}に着陸しようとすると、ジェームズは寝室に消える。船が着陸した後、彼は出てくる。これまで着ていた油汚れのついた作業着ではなく、スーツを着ている。{2}彼はうわの空でスーツの前を整え、どこに手を置けばいいのか分からないかのように自分の手を見つめる。「どう見える？」と彼は尋ねる。"

#. [ES10-0164] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2255
msgctxt "ES10-0164"
msgid "{1}\"Like a millionaire.\""
msgstr "{1}「百万長者みたいに見えるよ」"

#. [ES10-0165] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2257
msgctxt "ES10-0165"
msgid "{1}\"You look great.\""
msgstr "{1}「とても似合っているよ」"

#. [ES10-0166] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2261
msgctxt "ES10-0166"
msgid "{1}\"Well, that's the other thing about being a captain,\" he says. \"You can get filthy rich.\""
msgstr "{1}「ああ、船長になることのもう一つの利点だ」と彼は言う。「大金持ちになれるからな。」"

#. [ES10-0167] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2265
msgctxt "ES10-0167"
msgid "{1}\"Let's hope the locals think so,\" he says."
msgstr "{1}「地元の人々もそう思ってくれるといいんだが」と彼は言う。"

#. [ES10-0168] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2268
msgctxt "ES10-0168"
msgid "{1}There's an awkward pause. You're unsure of how to respond. Then he says, \"Thing is, this here planet is one of the most exclusive retirement communities in the galaxy. Plenty of the locals are probably worth more than a billion credits. But they're mostly financial or business types, or old money. I'm rich enough to be here, but I just hope they're willing to socialize with someone who made his fortune flying a ship."
msgstr "{1}気まずい沈黙が流れる。あなたはどう反応すべきか分からない。すると彼は言った。「実は、この惑星は銀河でも指折りの高級な引退者向け居住地なんだ。地元住民の多くは、おそらく10億クレジット以上の資産を持っているだろう。だが彼らのほとんどは金融やビジネス関係者、あるいは代々の資産家だ。私はここにいられるくらいには金持ちだが、船を操って財を成した人間と付き合ってくれるかどうか、ただそれだけが心配なんだ。」"

#. [ES10-0169] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2269
msgctxt "ES10-0169"
msgid "{1}\"Before you go, is there anything else you'd like to ask me about being a new pilot?\""
msgstr "{1}「行く前に、新米パイロットとして他に聞いておきたいことはあるか？」"

#. [ES10-0170] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2272
msgctxt "ES10-0170"
msgid "{1}\"Where should I go if I want to avoid pirates?\""
msgstr "{1}「海賊を避けるにはどこへ行けばいいですか？」"

#. [ES10-0171] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2275
msgctxt "ES10-0171"
msgid "{1}\"Have you ever met any aliens?\""
msgstr "{1}「これまでに異星人と会ったことはありますか？」"

#. [ES10-0172] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2279
msgctxt "ES10-0172"
msgid "{1}\"Are there any good trade routes you can give me?\""
msgstr "{1}「教えてもらえるような良い交易ルートはありますか？」"

#. [ES10-0173] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2283
msgctxt "ES10-0173"
msgid "{1}\"Where can I find well-paying jobs?\""
msgstr "{1}「どこで高収入の仕事を見つけられますか？」"

#. [ES10-0174] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2287
msgctxt "ES10-0174"
msgid "{1}\"I'm ready to go out on my own.\""
msgstr "{1}「一人立ちする準備はできています。」"

#. [ES10-0175] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2291
msgctxt "ES10-0175"
msgid "{1}\"Stay near Sol and around the Paradise Worlds. The Navy stays there the most, so even if a pirate does show up, they won't last long. The Deep is also a pretty safe place, as they have their own security forces. Once you start moving farther south, things get riskier. The worlds down there don't bring in as much tax revenue as the Paradise Worlds do, so the Navy tends to ignore them. You'll find some local militia to back you up, but they're nothing compared to one of the Navy's Cruisers."
msgstr "{1}「ソル近辺やパラダイス・ワールドの周辺に留まることだ。そこは海軍の駐留が最も手厚いから、たとえ海賊が現れても長くは持たないだろう。ディープも独自の治安部隊がいるのでかなり安全な場所だ。さらに南へ進むほど危険になる。あそこの惑星はパラダイス・ワールドほど税収をもたらさないため、海軍は無視する傾向がある。地元の民兵が支援してくれることもあるが、海軍の巡洋艦と比べれば大したことはない。」"

#. [ES10-0176] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2292
msgctxt "ES10-0176"
msgid "{1}\"If you do end up in pirate space, then sometimes the best defense is no defense at all. Pirates will prioritize fighting armed threats over unarmed transports, so if you don't install any weapons, you might be able to sneak away.\""
msgstr "{1}「もし海賊の領域に入ってしまったら、最善の防御は防御しないことだ。海賊は武装した脅威との戦闘を優先するため、武器を装備しなければ、こっそり逃げ出せるかもしれない。」"

#. [ES10-0177] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2298
msgctxt "ES10-0177"
msgid "{1}\"I've spoken with the Quarg a few times, but what captain hasn't? You'll find them down south by Tarazed. I haven't met any other aliens,\" he pauses for a moment, \"as far as I'm aware, that is, but I'm sure they're out there if you go looking hard enough. I've explored all of Republic space in my many years, but there are far more systems out there that we don't even know how to reach.\""
msgstr "{1}「クァーグとは何度か話したことがあるが、話したことのない船長などいるだろうか？彼らは南のタラゼドの近くにいる。他の異星人には会ったことがない」と彼は少し間を置く。「私が知る限りではね。だが、根気よく探せばきっとどこかにいるはずだ。私は長年かけて共和国領のすべてを探索してきたが、到達方法すら分からない星系がまだはるかに多くある。」"

#. [ES10-0178] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2304
msgctxt "ES10-0178"
msgid "{1}\"One of the most reliable trade routes is to bring food from the Dirt Belt to Earth or the other urban worlds around it. There are billions of mouths to feed on those worlds, and the Dirt Belt sells food for cheap, so it's a great place to get started. Just remember though that if you use the same trade route for too long, you might end up causing the prices to stabilize. The Dirt Belt can only produce food and people can only eat it so fast, so change up your trade routes if you notice the return getting worse.\""
msgstr "{1}「最も確実な交易ルートの一つは、ダートベルトから地球やその周辺の都市惑星へ食料を運ぶことだ。それらの惑星には何十億もの人々が暮らし、ダートベルトは食料を安く売っているから、交易を始めるには絶好のルートだ。ただし、同じ交易ルートを長く使いすぎると、価格が安定してしまう可能性があることを覚えておいてくれ。ダートベルトが食料を生産できる速さにも、人々がそれを消費できる速さにも限界がある。利益が減ってきたと感じたら、交易ルートを変えることだ。」"

#. [ES10-0179] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2310
msgctxt "ES10-0179"
msgid "{1}\"Getting good jobs is more about having the space to accept the good jobs than it is finding them, but if you're looking for jobs that pay well for little effort, then you'll want to watch out around the holidays. There's always a big celebration on Earth every April 22nd, Earth Day, so pay attention to the job board in the months leading up to that. The people down in the Rim have some month-long celebration every August that you should look out for too.\""
msgstr "{1}「良い仕事は見つけることよりも、受諾するための空き容量を確保しておくことの方が大事だ。だが、少ない労力で高収入の仕事を探しているなら、祝祭の時期に注意するといい。毎年4月22日のアースデイには地球で大きな祝祭があるから、その数か月前から求人掲示板に注目しておくことだ。リムの連中も毎年8月に1か月続く祝祭をやっているから、それにも注意しておくといい。」"

#. [ES10-0180] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "end of intro missions" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter; Interceptor; Transport (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <payment> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:2319
msgctxt "ES10-0180"
msgid "{1}James hands you a credit chip worth {2}, and says, \"Best of luck to you, Captain. Don't hesitate to look me up if you're ever in the area. And remember to check the spaceports wherever you land. You never know who you'll find wandering around there.\""
msgstr "{1}ジェームズは{2}相当のクレジットチップをあなたに手渡し、こう言う。「幸運を祈るよ、船長。この辺りに来ることがあれば、遠慮なく訪ねてくれ。それから、どこに着陸しても宇宙港を覗いてみるのを忘れるな。誰がそこをぶらついているか分からないからな。」"

#. [ES10-0181] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 1 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <commodity>; <planet>; <payment> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:152
msgctxt "ES10-0181"
msgid "You drop off the shipment of {1} on {2}, and collect your payment of {3}. \"Hauling freight,\" says James. \"Not the most glamorous job, or the most interesting, but you're always guaranteed steady income. And once you know the galaxy a bit better, instead of taking missions you can find your own trade routes to follow. The only trouble is, build up a fleet with lots of cargo space and not enough defenses and the pirates begin to take notice.\""
msgstr "あなたは{2}で{1}の貨物を届け、{3}の報酬を受け取る。「貨物輸送か」とジェームズは言う。「最も華やかな仕事でも、最も興味深い仕事でもないが、安定した収入は常に保証されている。銀河のことがもう少し分かってくれば、ミッションを受ける代わりに、自分で交易ルートを見つけて回ることもできる。唯一の問題は、積載量は多いが防御力が足りない艦隊を組むと、海賊に目をつけられることだ。」"

#. [ES10-0182] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 1 end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:154
msgctxt "ES10-0182"
msgid "{1}\"Did you have a lot of trouble with pirates when you were a captain?\""
msgstr "{1}「あなたが船長だった頃、海賊にはずいぶん悩まされましたか？」"

#. [ES10-0183] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 1 end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:155
msgctxt "ES10-0183"
msgid "{1}\"But what if I want to earn money more quickly than I can by trading?\""
msgstr "{1}「でも、交易で稼ぐよりも早くお金を稼ぎたい場合はどうすればいいですか？」"

#. [ES10-0184] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 1 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:157
msgctxt "ES10-0184"
msgid "{1}\"Some. That's why you can't just go traipsing around the galaxy in a fleet of unarmed star barges; every pirate within a week's travel will hear you're coming through and come after you. In the long term, having a few heavy freighters with good defenses is more cost-effective than losing a star barge or two to the pirates on every journey.\""
msgstr "{1}「多少はね。だから、武装していないスターバージの船団で銀河をのんきにうろついてはいけないんだ。1週間の移動圏内にいる海賊はみんな、君が通りかかると聞きつけて襲ってくる。長い目で見れば、防御力の高い大型貨物船を数隻持っておく方が、旅のたびに海賊にスターバージを1、2隻奪われるよりも費用対効果が高いんだ」"

#. [ES10-0185] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 1 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:160
msgctxt "ES10-0185"
msgid "{1}\"There's no quick road to riches, kid. The more something pays, the riskier it is. If you need to make lots of money in a hurry, bounty hunting is the way to go, but nine out of ten pilots who give bounty hunting a try end up dead. And no one's going to give you those sorts of missions until you've proved yourself in combat, anyway.\""
msgstr "{1}「金持ちへの近道なんてないよ、若いの。儲かるものほどリスクが高い。急いで大金を稼ぐ必要があるなら賞金稼ぎが一番だが、賞金稼ぎに挑戦するパイロットの10人中9人は死ぬことになる。それに、戦闘で実力を証明するまでは、誰もそんな任務をくれないだろうしね」"

#. [ES10-0186] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 1 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:162
msgctxt "ES10-0186"
msgid "{1}He picks up his suitcase. \"If you want to run another mission with me, look for me in the spaceport. I'll see if I can find you something with a higher profit margin this time.\""
msgstr "{1}彼はスーツケースを手に取る。「もし私と別の任務をこなしたいなら、宇宙港で私を探してくれ。次はもっと利益率の高い仕事を見つけられるか試してみるよ」"

#. [ES10-0188] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet>; <payment> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:169
msgctxt "ES10-0188"
msgid "By now, your entire ship smells like brine and raw fish, but as best you can tell the fish is still fresh enough to eat. The dock workers on {1} offload it without comment, and give you your payment of {2}."
msgstr "今や船内全体に塩水と生魚の臭いが漂っているが、分かる限りでは魚はまだ食べられるほど新鮮だ。{1}のドック作業員は何も言わずに荷降ろしをし、{2}の報酬を支払ってくれる。"

#. [ES10-0189] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet>; <payment> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:174
msgctxt "ES10-0189"
msgid "Your cargo has loomed silently in your hold for the last few days, but as far as you can tell, the samples are still safely contained. The dock workers on {1} offload it without comment, and give you your payment of {2}."
msgstr "貨物はここ数日、船倉で静かに鎮座していたが、分かる限りではサンプルはまだ容器の中に安全に収まっている。{1}のドック作業員は何も言わずに荷降ろしをし、{2}の報酬を支払ってくれる。"

#. [ES10-0190] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet>; <payment> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:177
msgctxt "ES10-0190"
msgid "Your cargo has loomed silently in your hold for the last few days, but the radiation alarms in your ship's hold haven't let out a squeak. The dock workers on {1} offload it quickly onto several waiting trains, and give you your payment of {2}."
msgstr "貨物はここ数日、船倉で静かに鎮座していたが、船倉の放射線警報器は一度も鳴っていない。{1}のドック作業員はそれを素早く待機中の数台の列車に積み込み、{2}の報酬を支払ってくれる。"

#. [ES10-0191] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:181
msgctxt "ES10-0191"
msgid "{1}\"If you can line them up right,\" says James, \"rush deliveries can be your best source of income as a freighter captain. And keep your eye out for missions with large amounts of cargo, too, because your barge's hold is definitely big enough to handle them. And if you've got any cargo space to spare and you know what the prices are going to be at your destination, be sure to stock up on something you can sell for a profit.\""
msgstr "{1}「うまく段取りを組めれば」とジェームズは言う。「急ぎの配送は、貨物船の船長にとって最高の収入源になる。それと、大量の貨物を運ぶ任務にも目を光らせておくといい。君のバージの船倉なら十分な広さがあるはずだからね。もし貨物スペースに余裕があって、目的地での価格が分かっているなら、利益が出るものを買い込んでおくのを忘れないように」"

#. [ES10-0192] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:183
msgctxt "ES10-0192"
msgid "{1}\"What would you recommend if I want to do more than just carry cargo?\""
msgstr "{1}「荷物を運ぶ以外のこともしたい場合、何をおすすめしますか？」"

#. [ES10-0193] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:184
msgctxt "ES10-0193"
msgid "{1}\"Did you do that for your whole career?\""
msgstr "{1}「仕事をしていた間、ずっとそれを続けていたのですか？」"

#. [ES10-0194] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:186
msgctxt "ES10-0194"
msgid "{1}He pauses for a moment to think, then says, \"Unless you want to do something really risky like hunting pirates, your best bet is to work with the Navy, or the Syndicate, or one of the local militias. Any of those would be a decent choice, although they've each got their own problems. If any of them offer you a mission, go ahead and take it; that's a good way to build connections and get to know the lay of the land.\""
msgstr "{1}彼は少し考えてから言った。「海賊狩りのような本当に危険なことをしたいのでなければ、海軍やシンジケート、あるいは地元の民兵組織と協力するのが一番だ。どれを選んでも悪くはないが、それぞれに問題はある。もし彼らから任務を依頼されたら、引き受けるといい。人脈を築き、状況を把握するのに良い方法だからね」"

#. [ES10-0195] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:189
msgctxt "ES10-0195"
msgid "{1}\"Well,\" he says, \"Back when I was a bit older than you, I piloted a Firebird for a while, escorting merchant convoys up and down the Rim. I used to hope we'd get attacked; I'd disable the pirate ships and rob them blind. Turnabout is fair play, after all."
msgstr "{1}「そうだな」と彼は言う。「君より少し年上だった頃、私はしばらくファイアバードを操縦して、リムのあちこちで商船団の護衛をしていた。襲撃されることを期待していたものさ。海賊船を無力化して、丸裸にしてやるためにね。結局のところ、やられたらやり返すのが公平というものだ」"

#. [ES10-0196] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:190
msgctxt "ES10-0196"
msgid "{1}\"Then one day I got a bit too greedy and thought I'd try to capture a pirate ship or two, to add more firepower to my fleet. We boarded their ship, and I sent my crew through the airlock to kill off the pirates. And it turns out the pirates had grenades. Four of my men were dead before I even realized what was happening. We had to retreat, and then limp back to port without even enough crew left uninjured to pilot the ship right. After that I decided to stick to less risky jobs.\""
msgstr "{1}「ところがある日、少し欲を出しすぎて、海賊船を1、2隻拿捕して艦隊の火力を強化しようと考えた。彼らの船に乗り込み、海賊を殺すために乗組員をエアロックから送り込んだんだ。ところが、海賊は手榴弾を持っていた。何が起きているのか理解する前に、部下の4人が死んでいた。私たちは撤退を余儀なくされ、船をまともに操縦するのに必要な数の無傷の乗組員も残っていない状態で、なんとか港まで戻った。それ以来、リスクの低い仕事に専念することにしたよ」"

#. [ES10-0197] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "freighter 2 end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:192
msgctxt "ES10-0197"
msgid "{1}He glances toward the spaceport and says, \"Anyway, if you want to make one more trip with me, you know where to find me.\""
msgstr "{1}彼は宇宙港の方を見て言う。「とにかく、もう一度私と旅をしたいなら、どこへ来ればいいか分かっているね」"

#. [ES10-0198] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro ingot" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:197
msgctxt "ES10-0198"
msgid "You find James talking with a group of miners, who seem to be old acquaintances of his. As you approach, he says, \"Well guys, here comes my ride. I should probably say goodbye.\" They head back off to do their work. \"Every time I land here,\" says James, \"I'm amazed that this station hasn't been wiped out yet by a meteorite. Can you imagine spending your life here?\""
msgstr "あなたはジェームズが旧知の仲らしい鉱山労働者の一団と話しているのを見つける。あなたが近づくと、彼は「さてみんな、迎えが来たようだ。そろそろお別れだな」と言う。彼らは仕事に戻っていく。「ここに着陸するたびに」とジェームズは言う。「このステーションがまだ隕石で消滅していないことに驚かされるよ。ここで一生を過ごすなんて想像できるか？」"

#. [ES10-0199] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro ingot" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:199
msgctxt "ES10-0199"
msgid "{1}\"It does seem awfully isolated. But some people might enjoy the solitude.\""
msgstr "{1}「確かにずいぶん辺鄙な場所ですね。でも、人里離れた暮らしを楽しむ人もいるかもしれません」"

#. [ES10-0200] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro ingot" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:200
msgctxt "ES10-0200"
msgid "{1}\"Well, if you need the money, at least it's a steady job.\""
msgstr "{1}「まあ、お金が必要なら、少なくとも安定した仕事ではありますね」"

#. [ES10-0201] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro ingot" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:201
msgctxt "ES10-0201"
msgid "{1}\"I suppose,\" he says. \"Anyway, I think it's time for the last leg of my journey. Do you think you can give me a lift to {2}? I'll pay you quite well for your services, of course.\""
msgstr "{1}「そうだな」と彼は言う。「とにかく、旅の最後の行程に向かう時間だ。{2}まで乗せていってくれないか？もちろん、報酬はしっかり払うよ」"

#. [ES10-0202] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro ingot" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:203
msgctxt "ES10-0202"
msgid "{1}\"I can take you there.\""
msgstr "{1}「そこまでお送りします」"

#. [ES10-0203] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "intro ingot" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Freighter (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:204
msgctxt "ES10-0203"
msgid "{1}\"Sorry, I was thinking of heading in a different direction from here.\""
msgstr "{1}「すみません、ここからは別の方向へ向かおうと考えていたんです」"

#. [ES10-0205] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor escort end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <npc>; <payment>; <their>; <they're> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:212
msgctxt "ES10-0205"
msgid "The captain of the {1} hands you {2} and thanks you for your escort services. From the expression on {3} face, you'd guess that {4} feeling lucky to still be alive after entrusting the safety of {5} fleet to a rookie pilot like yourself."
msgstr "{1}の船長はあなたに{2}を手渡し、護衛の礼を言う。{3}の表情から察するに、あなたのような新米パイロットに{5}の船団の安全を委ねた後も無事でいられたことを、{4}幸運だと感じているのだろう。"

#. [ES10-0206] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor escort end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <they are> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:213
msgctxt "ES10-0206"
msgid "{1}After {2} gone, James turns to you and says, \"Not too bad for your first escort mission. I recognize that look on your face - it's the same one I had after my first job like this back when I was a beginner. If I recall, my first priority after touching down was replacing some of the ship's guns with missile launchers so I'd actually have a chance against pirates. It's a scandal how they sell interceptors with nothing but short-ranged energy weapons these days; trying to use them in combat on such a small ship is practically suicide. Keep your distance with some missiles and you can almost never go wrong."
msgstr "{1}{2}が去った後、ジェームズはあなたの方を向いて言う。「初めての護衛任務にしては悪くない。その顔つきには見覚えがあるよ。私が駆け出しの頃、初めてこの手の仕事をした後も同じ顔をしていた。確か、着陸して真っ先にやったのは、海賊に対抗できるように船の砲の一部をミサイルランチャーに換装することだったな。最近は短射程のエネルギー兵器しか積んでいない迎撃機を売っているなんて言語道断だ。そんな小さな船でその兵器を使って戦おうとするのは、自殺行為に等しい。ミサイルを使って距離を保てば、まず間違いないよ」"

#. [ES10-0207] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor escort end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:215
msgctxt "ES10-0207"
msgid "{1}\"Anyway, I'll stop rambling. If you've still got a hankering for some dangerous missions, come and find me in the spaceport before you leave.\" He picks up his suitcase and heads outside."
msgstr "{1}「とにかく、長話はやめよう。まだ危険な任務に興味があるなら、出発する前に宇宙港で私を探してくれ」彼はスーツケースを手に取り、外へ向かう。"

#. [ES10-0208] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor escort end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:218
msgctxt "ES10-0208"
msgid "{1}\"Anyway, I'll stop rambling.\" James pauses for a moment, then says, \"I've got an idea for something you might want to try. Meet me in the spaceport bar in a little while.\""
msgstr "{1}「とにかく、長話はやめよう」ジェームズは少し間を置いてから言う。「君が試してみたいと思うかもしれないことを思いついたんだ。少ししたら宇宙港のバーで会おう」"

#. [ES10-0209] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor escort end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:227
msgctxt "ES10-0209"
msgid "{1}(As before, click the \"Spaceport\" button to continue this mission. The next mission will involve carrying cargo, so it will only show up if you have 10 tons of space free.)"
msgstr "{1}（以前と同様に、「宇宙港」ボタンをクリックしてこの任務を続けてください。次の任務は貨物の輸送を伴うため、積載容量に10トン分の空きがある場合にのみ表示されます。）"

#. [ES10-0210] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor escort end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:232
msgctxt "ES10-0210"
msgid "{1}(The next mission will involve carrying a passenger, so it will only show up if you have all your bunks free.)"
msgstr "{1}（次の任務は乗客の輸送を伴うため、すべての寝台が空いている場合にのみ表示されます。）"

#. [ES10-0211] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:245
msgctxt "ES10-0211"
msgid "You find James in the spaceport bar, talking with a woman wearing a business suit. The expression on James' face is growing increasingly concerned as she speaks. Seeing you come in, he waves to you and you join them at the table."
msgstr "あなたは宇宙港のバーで、ビジネススーツを着た女性と話しているジェームズを見つける。彼女が話すにつれて、ジェームズの表情はますます険しくなっていく。あなたが入ってくるのに気づいた彼は手を振り、あなたも二人のいるテーブルに加わる。"

#. [ES10-0212] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:246
msgctxt "ES10-0212"
msgid "{1}\"Hello {2},\" says James. \"This is Marissa, a senior manager at the mines.\" You shake hands with her."
msgstr "{1}「やあ、{2}」とジェームズが言う。「こちらは鉱山のシニアマネージャー、マリッサだ」あなたは彼女と握手する。"

#. [ES10-0213] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:247
msgctxt "ES10-0213"
msgid "{1}\"Here's the deal,\" says Marissa. \"Most of the gemstones we mine here are industrial grade, not pretty enough to be worth using as anything but sandpaper grit or drill bits. But every once in a while we happen on some higher quality gems. No one in this sector has the money to spend on jewelry, so we ship them north to the Paradise Worlds."
msgstr "{1}「話はこうです」とマリッサは言います。「私たちがここで採掘する宝石のほとんどは工業用で、サンドペーパーの研磨材やドリルビットにする以外に使えるほど見栄えが良くありません。ですが、時折、より高品質な宝石が見つかることがあります。このセクターには宝飾品にお金をかけられる人はいませんので、そうした宝石は北のパラダイス・ワールドへ出荷しているのです」"

#. [ES10-0214] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <ship> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:248
msgctxt "ES10-0214"
msgid "{1}\"But in the past few months, every shipment we've sent has been attacked by a pirate ship, the Hammer of Thor. We don't have the money to pay a bounty hunter to take out the Hammer, so instead we're going to pay you to outrun it. Is the {2} a fast ship?\""
msgstr "{1}「しかしここ数ヶ月、私たちが送った貨物はすべて、海賊船『トールのハンマー』に襲撃されています。『トールのハンマー』を排除するために賞金稼ぎを雇う資金はありません。ですから代わりに、あなたに報酬を払って、それを振り切ってもらおうと考えています。{2}は速い船ですか？」"

#. [ES10-0215] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:250
msgctxt "ES10-0215"
msgid "{1}\"As fast as they come. Nothing bigger than a fighter could chase it down.\""
msgstr "{1}「最高に速いですよ。戦闘機より大きい船なら、追いつけるものはありません。」"

#. [ES10-0216] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:251
msgctxt "ES10-0216"
msgid "{1}\"Not fast enough. I don't think I can risk taking on this mission.\""
msgstr "{1}「それほど速くはありません。この任務を引き受ける危険は冒せそうにありません」"

#. [ES10-0217] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:253
msgctxt "ES10-0217"
msgid "{1}\"Great,\" she says. \"My people will load up your ship immediately. Good luck, Captain.\""
msgstr "{1}「素晴らしい」と彼女は言う。「すぐに船に積み込ませます。幸運を祈ります、船長」"

#. [ES10-0218] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:257
msgctxt "ES10-0218"
msgid "You end up finding James in a bar talking to a woman in a military uniform. \"Nice to see you, {1},\" he says. \"I've been talking to Lieutenant Engberg over here, and I think we have a job on our hands.\""
msgstr "あなたはジェームズがバーで軍服を着た女性と話しているのを見つける。「会えてうれしいよ、{1}」と彼は言う。「こちらのエングバーグ中尉と話していたんだが、どうやら私たちに仕事がありそうだ」"

#. [ES10-0219] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. [ES10-0230] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:279
msgctxt "ES10-0219"
msgid "{1}\"What is it?\""
msgstr "{1}「どんな仕事ですか？」"

#. [ES10-0220] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. [ES10-0231] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:281
msgctxt "ES10-0220"
msgid "{1}\"You haven't drafted me into the Navy, have you?\""
msgstr "{1}「まさか、私を海軍に徴兵しようというわけじゃないですよね？」"

#. [ES10-0221] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. [ES10-0232] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:282
msgctxt "ES10-0221"
msgid "{1}\"Actually, I want to go out on my own now.\""
msgstr "{1}「実は、今は自分一人でやっていきたいんです。」"

#. [ES10-0222] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:264
msgctxt "ES10-0222"
msgid "{1}Engberg chuckles. \"Firstly, I'm not part of the Navy, I'm with Deep Security. And secondly, not to disparage your abilities, but we only recruit experienced captains into our ranks.\""
msgstr "{1}エングバーグはくすりと笑う。「第一に、私は海軍ではなくディープ・セキュリティの所属です。第二に、あなたの能力をけなすつもりはありませんが、我々は経験豊富な船長しか採用していません」"

#. [ES10-0223] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:266
msgctxt "ES10-0223"
msgid "{1}James says, \"Deep Security mainly acts as the Deep equivalent of the Navy, protecting merchants from pirates. However, they also deal with the transport of confidential documents and equipment, for both the private and government sector.\""
msgstr "{1}ジェームズが言う。「ディープ・セキュリティは主にディープにおける海軍のような役割を担い、海賊から商船を守っている。だが、民間と政府の両方のために、機密文書や機材の輸送も扱っているんだ」"

#. [ES10-0224] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <ship> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:267
msgctxt "ES10-0224"
msgid "{1}Engberg continues. \"Recently, one of our logistics ships was attacked and damaged by a merchant warship named the Arm of Odin. We now believe that ship to be a pirate vessel in disguise, specifically targeting the cargo onboard. We're looking for a replacement ship capable of avoiding the threat while we track down the warlord. How fast would you say the {2} is?\""
msgstr "{1}エングバーグは続ける。「最近、我々の輸送船の一隻が、『アーム・オブ・オーディン』という武装商船に攻撃され、損傷しました。現在、その船は商船を装った海賊船で、積荷を狙っていたと考えています。我々がその海賊船を追跡する間、脅威を回避できる代わりの船を探しています。{2}の速度はどの程度ですか？」"

#. [ES10-0225] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. [ES10-0236] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:289
msgctxt "ES10-0225"
msgid "{1}\"It'll outspeed anything short of a fighter.\""
msgstr "{1}「戦闘機を除けば、どんな船よりも速いですよ」"

#. [ES10-0226] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. [ES10-0237] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:290
msgctxt "ES10-0226"
msgid "{1}\"Not fast enough. You'll have to find someone else for the job.\""
msgstr "{1}「速さが足りません。この仕事はほかの人に頼んでください」"

#. [ES10-0227] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:272
msgctxt "ES10-0227"
msgid "{1}\"Good,\" she says. \"We'll have the cargo loaded onto your ship by sundown.\""
msgstr "{1}「いいでしょう」と彼女は言う。「日没までにあなたの船に貨物を積み込みます」"

#. [ES10-0228] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <origin> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:276
msgctxt "ES10-0228"
msgid "For a planet so close to the Paradise Worlds, {1} could not be any more different. Where the Paradise Worlds have meticulously preplanned cities, {2} was designed by immediate needs. Where the Paradise Worlds cover themselves with nature and sculptures, {3} bares itself to the galaxy, indulging in concrete pillars and steel trusses. Where the Paradise Worlds believe themselves to be untouchable utopias, {4} is hardly afraid to show the scars of battle, its turrets and Navy garrisons in full display."
msgstr "パラダイス・ワールドにこれほど近い惑星でありながら、{1}はこれ以上ないほど対照的だ。パラダイス・ワールドには綿密に計画された都市がある一方、{2}はその場その場の必要に応じて造られた。パラダイス・ワールドが自然や彫刻で身を包む一方、{3}はコンクリートの柱や鋼鉄のトラスを誇示し、銀河にありのままの姿をさらしている。パラダイス・ワールドが自らを誰にも手出しできない理想郷だと信じる一方、{4}は戦いの傷跡を隠そうともせず、砲塔や海軍の駐屯地を堂々と見せている。"

#. [ES10-0229] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:277
msgctxt "ES10-0229"
msgid "{1}You end up finding James in one of the cleaner bars, talking to a man in a Navy uniform. \"Nice to see you, {2},\" he says. \"I've been talking to Lieutenant Armen over here, and I think we have a job on our hands.\""
msgstr "{1}あなたは比較的きれいなバーの一つで、海軍の制服を着た男と話しているジェームズを見つける。「会えて嬉しいよ、{2}」と彼は言う。「ここにいるアルメン中尉と話していたんだが、どうやら俺たちに仕事ができたようだ」"

#. [ES10-0233] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:284
msgctxt "ES10-0233"
msgid "{1}Armen grins. \"You would have a lot more to do if you were joining the Navy.\""
msgstr "{1}アルメンはにやりと笑う。「海軍に入ってくれれば、もっとたくさん仕事があるんだがな」"

#. [ES10-0234] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:286
msgctxt "ES10-0234"
msgid "{1}James says, \"More than ever, the Republic Navy is struggling to hold off the threat of piracy. While they are able to keep the Paradise Worlds safe, on the edges of the known galaxy, pirates readily outnumber Navy forces. There are more ways to stop piracy than sheer force, however.\""
msgstr "{1}ジェームズは言う。「共和国海軍は今、かつてないほど海賊の脅威を食い止めるのに苦戦している。楽園惑星の安全は守れているが、既知の銀河の辺境では海賊の数が海軍の戦力をたやすく上回っている。だが、海賊行為を阻止する手段は武力だけじゃない」"

#. [ES10-0235] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <ship> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:287
msgctxt "ES10-0235"
msgid "{1}Armen continues. \"Which is where you come in. Recently, we've come into contact with someone claiming to have information on pirate activity in the North. If they're telling the truth, their knowledge could open the way for preemptive strikes against the pirates, freeing ships to be deployed elsewhere. However, the informant's existence has leaked, and a hired ship named the Eye of Loki is trying to cover up this loose end. We're looking for a ship able to outspeed the Eye and bring the informant safely to Pearl; we can handle transport from there. How fast would you say the {2} is?\""
msgstr "{1}アルメンが続ける。「そこで君の出番だ。最近、北方での海賊の活動について情報を持っているという人物と接触した。そいつの言うことが本当なら、その情報をもとに海賊に先制攻撃を仕掛け、艦船をほかの場所に回せるようになる。だが、情報提供者の存在が漏れ、アイ・オブ・ロキという雇われ船が口封じを図っている。我々はアイ・オブ・ロキより速く、情報提供者を無事にパールまで送り届けられる船を探している。そこから先の輸送は我々が引き受ける。君の{2}はどれくらい速い？」"

#. [ES10-0238] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:292
msgctxt "ES10-0238"
msgid "{1}\"Good,\" he says. \"I'll have the informant on your ship by sundown.\""
msgstr "{1}「よし」と彼は言う。「日没までには情報提供者を君の船に乗せよう」"

#. [ES10-0239] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:296
msgctxt "ES10-0239"
msgid "You find James in the spaceport bar, talking with a man wearing a business suit. The expression on James' face is growing increasingly concerned as he speaks. Seeing you come in, he waves to you and you join them at the table."
msgstr "あなたは宇宙港のバーで、スーツ姿の男と話しているジェームズを見つける。話すうちに、ジェームズの表情はますます険しくなっていく。あなたが入ってきたのに気づくと、彼は手を振る。あなたは二人のいるテーブルに加わる。"

#. [ES10-0240] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first>; <origin> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:297
msgctxt "ES10-0240"
msgid "{1}\"Hello {2},\" says James. \"This is Miguel, an independent mine owner on {3}.\" Miguel smiles at you."
msgstr "{1}「やあ、{2}」とジェームズが言う。「こちらはミゲルだ。{3}の独立系の鉱山主だよ」ミゲルはあなたに微笑みかける。"

#. [ES10-0241] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <origin> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:298
msgctxt "ES10-0241"
msgid "{1}\"Here's the deal,\" says Miguel. \"Most of the mining companies on {2} have ties to the Syndicate, whether that be through direct ownership or indirect influence. Not us, though; my company's been resistant to any attempts of a takeover. One of their controlling techniques is preventing us from shipping our minerals to refineries within the Syndicate. However, there's nothing stopping us from shipping materials elsewhere in the galaxy, like magnetic elements for Lovelace's particle accelerators.\""
msgstr "{1}「事情を説明します」とミゲルは言う。「{2}にある鉱山会社のほとんどは、直接所有されているか、間接的に影響を受けているかの違いこそあれ、シンジケートとつながりがあります。でも、うちは違います。私の会社は、これまであらゆる買収の試みを退けてきました。彼らの支配手法の一つは、我々がシンジケート内の精錬所に鉱物を輸送するのを妨げることです。ですが、銀河のほかの場所へ物資を輸送することまでは止められません。ラブレスの粒子加速器に使う磁性元素などですね」"

#. [ES10-0242] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:299
msgctxt "ES10-0242"
msgid "{1}\"But in the past few months, every shipment we've sent has been attacked by a pirate ship, the Spear of Heimdall. I doubt Syndicated Security would be keen on helping a rival company, so instead we're going to pay you to outrun it. Can you do that for us?\""
msgstr "{1}「しかしここ数か月、我々が送った貨物はすべて『ヘイムダルの槍』という海賊船に襲撃されています。シンジケーテッド・セキュリティが競合他社を助けたがるとは思えませんので、代わりにあなたに報酬を支払い、その船を振り切ってもらいたいのです。我々のためにそれをやっていただけますか？」"

#. [ES10-0243] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:301
msgctxt "ES10-0243"
msgid "{1}\"If you're willing to pay, I'm willing to fly.\""
msgstr "{1}「報酬を払ってくれるなら、喜んで飛ぶよ」"

#. [ES10-0244] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:302
msgctxt "ES10-0244"
msgid "{1}\"I got into the starship business to get away from people like you. Count me out.\""
msgstr "{1}「あんたみたいな人間と関わりたくなくて、宇宙船の仕事を始めたんだ。俺は降りるよ」"

#. [ES10-0245] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:304
msgctxt "ES10-0245"
msgid "{1}\"Great,\" he says. \"My people will load up your ship immediately. Good luck, Captain.\""
msgstr "{1}「よかった」と彼は言う。「私の部下がすぐにあなたの船に積み込みを行います。幸運を祈ります、船長」"

#. [ES10-0246] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <person>; <enemy>; <magnitude> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:307
msgctxt "ES10-0246"
msgid "{1}After {2} leaves, James says to you, \"Now, get one thing clear. This is not your David and Goliath moment. The {3}'s shields are {4} times as strong as yours, and if it's able to bring its weapons to bear, we'll be dead in two seconds. So, the moment we're in the sky, we head straight for hyperspace. Don't even wait around to see if the {5} is coming or not. Got it?\""
msgstr "{1}{2}が去った後、ジェームズはあなたに言う。「いいか、一つはっきりさせておく。これは君がダビデになってゴリアテを倒すような話じゃない。{3}のシールドは君の船のシールドの{4}倍の強度がある。あいつに攻撃態勢を取られたら、俺たちは2秒でお陀仏だ。だから、空に出たらすぐにハイパースペースへ直行する。{5}が追ってくるかどうかなんて確かめずにな。わかったか？」"

#. [ES10-0247] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:309
msgctxt "ES10-0247"
msgid "{1}\"Got it.\""
msgstr "{1}「了解」"

#. [ES10-0248] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:311
msgctxt "ES10-0248"
msgid "{1}\"I really shouldn't try to fight?\""
msgstr "{1}「本当に戦っちゃだめなのか？」"

#. [ES10-0249] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <model> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:312
msgctxt "ES10-0249"
msgid "{1}\"It just isn't feasible,\" he says. \"If a ship has turrets, your {2} can't get close enough to hit it with your guns without being damaged, and then it's just a matter of whose weapons and shields are stronger. If it has anti-missile turrets, you can't count on hanging back and bombarding it with missiles from long distances, or at least not with weapons that can fit in a {3}. So, don't risk it."
msgstr "{1}「勝ち目がないんだ」と彼は言う。「相手の船に砲塔があれば、君の{2}では損傷を受けずに船の砲の射程まで近づけない。そうなると、武器とシールドの性能勝負だ。対ミサイル砲塔まであれば、距離を取ってミサイルを撃ち続ける手も使えない。少なくとも{3}に搭載できる武器ではな。だから、危険を冒すな」"

#. [ES10-0250] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:313
msgctxt "ES10-0250"
msgid "{1}\"It's like rock paper scissors; recognize what your enemy's strengths and weaknesses are, as well as your own.\""
msgstr "{1}「じゃんけんのようなものだ。敵の強みと弱み、それに自分自身の強みと弱みも見極めるんだ」"

#. [ES10-0251] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:319
msgctxt "ES10-0251"
msgid "As you land on {1}, James says, \"Well, you made it in one piece! Still think you want to be piloting an interceptor?\""
msgstr "{1}に着陸すると、ジェームズが言う。「やれやれ、無事に着いたな！まだ迎撃機のパイロットになりたいと思っているのか？」"

#. [ES10-0252] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:321
msgctxt "ES10-0252"
msgid "{1}\"Sure, but I can't wait until I've got a ship big enough to stand up to pirates instead of running from them.\""
msgstr "{1}「もちろん。でも、海賊から逃げ回るんじゃなく、海賊に立ち向かえるくらい大きな船を手に入れるのが待ち遠しいよ」"

#. [ES10-0253] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:322
msgctxt "ES10-0253"
msgid "{1}\"Well, maybe I should've bought a freighter instead.\""
msgstr "{1}「まあ、貨物船を買っておくべきだったかもしれないな」"

#. [ES10-0254] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <commodity>; <planet>; <payment> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:323
msgctxt "ES10-0254"
msgid "{1}\"Better start saving up then,\" he says. \"I know a number of old Sparrow pilots who made their first million credits mining asteroids before they could afford a more combat-worthy ship. They had to look around for a while before finding a system with any asteroids worth mining, but it was worth it. Anyway, let's go get your payment.\" You walk out of the ship and sign the papers to hand off the {2} to the dock workers on {3}. They hand you a credit chip worth {4}."
msgstr "{1}「それなら、貯金を始めたほうがいいな」と彼は言う。「戦闘に適した船を買えるようになる前に、小惑星を採掘して最初の100万クレジットを稼いだスパローのパイロットを何人も知っている。彼らは採掘する価値のある小惑星がある星系を見つけるまで、しばらく探し回らなければならなかったが、それだけの価値はあった。とにかく、報酬を受け取りに行こう」あなたは船から降り、{3}のドック作業員に{2}を引き渡すための書類に署名する。彼らはあなたに{4}相当のクレジットチップを手渡す。"

#. [ES10-0255] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:324
msgctxt "ES10-0255"
msgid "{1}\"I've got an idea for something you might want to try,\" says James. \"Meet me in the spaceport bar in a little while.\""
msgstr "{1}「君が試してみたくなるようなことを思いついたんだ」とジェームズは言う。「少ししたら宇宙港のバーで会おう」"

#. [ES10-0256] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "interceptor evade end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:327
msgctxt "ES10-0256"
msgid "{1}\"I've got an idea for something you might want to try,\" says James. \"Meet me in the spaceport bar in a little while. And make sure you have a weapon installed; you should be able to buy one in {2}'s outfitter.\""
msgstr "{1}「君が試してみたくなるようなことを思いついたんだ」とジェームズは言う。「少ししたら宇宙港のバーで会おう。それと、武器を装備しておくのを忘れないように。{2}の装備屋で買えるはずだ」"

#. [ES10-0257] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <origin> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:336
msgctxt "ES10-0257"
msgid "You find James waiting for you just outside the spaceport bar. Against the steady patter of micrometeorites against the roof he tells you, \"Working here on {1} is one of the few jobs in the galaxy more dangerous than fighting pirates. And worse, because if a big meteorite decides to strike this station, there's basically nothing the miners can do about it except hope they see it coming.\" He turns to you with a grin. \"But nonetheless, I think you might be interested in this idea.\""
msgstr "あなたは宇宙港のバーのすぐ外で、ジェームズが待っているのを見つける。屋根を叩く微小隕石の絶え間ない音を背景に、彼はあなたに言う。「この{1}で働くのは、銀河系で海賊と戦うよりも危険な数少ない仕事の一つだ。さらに厄介なことに、大きな隕石がこのステーションに衝突しそうになったら、採掘者たちは事前に気づけるよう祈ることくらいしかできないんだ」彼はニヤリと笑ってあなたの方を向く。「だがそれでも、君はこのアイデアに興味を持つと思うよ」"

#. [ES10-0258] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <origin> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:339
msgctxt "ES10-0258"
msgid "Similar to Delve, {1}'s spaceport is embedded in solid rock, but that is where the similarities end. Where Delve's spaceport was utilitarian, Ada finds space to flex its wealth by turning the industrial elements of rock and metal into elegant architecture. The nightmarish take-off and landing angles one might expect from a spaceport set in a canyon wall are missing, replaced by spacious and well-marked flight paths. The smell of oil and steel pervasive in many Syndicate ports is suppressed by crisp air supplied by the local environmental control systems."
msgstr "デルヴと同様に、{1}の宇宙港は固い岩盤の中に埋め込まれているが、似ているのはそこまでだ。デルヴの宇宙港が実用本位だったのに対し、エイダは岩と金属という工業的な素材を優美な建築に変え、その豊かさを見せつけている。峡谷の壁に設けられた宇宙港から想像されるような恐ろしい角度での離着陸は必要なく、代わりに広々とした、目印の分かりやすい飛行経路が整備されている。多くのシンジケートの港に染みついた油と鋼鉄の臭いは、現地の環境制御システムが送り込む澄んだ空気によって抑えられている。"

#. [ES10-0259] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:342
msgctxt "ES10-0259"
msgid "{1}James leads you down the side of the bar to a booth where a man with a half-eaten hamburger and a plate of fries is sitting, busily examining a star map of the local sector. He notices your arrival and stands up to greet you. \"{2}, this is Captain Marshall,\" James says as you shake his hand. \"I told him about your new ship and how it'd be a good idea for you to get a taste of asteroid mining. He mines in this part of space and says there's a good system nearby if you're willing to give it a try.\""
msgstr "{1}ジェームズはあなたをバーの脇のブースへと案内する。そこには、食べかけのハンバーガーとフライドポテトの皿を前に、この宙域の星図を熱心に調べている男が座っている。彼はあなたの到着に気づき、立ち上がって挨拶する。「{2}、こちらはマーシャル船長だ」と、あなたが握手を交わす間、ジェームズが言う。「君の新しい船のことを話して、小惑星採掘を体験してみるといいんじゃないかと伝えておいた。彼はこの宙域で採掘をしていて、君が試してみたいなら、近くにいい星系があると言っているよ」"

#. [ES10-0260] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <origin> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:346
msgctxt "ES10-0260"
msgid "The world of {1} is in full bloom; the fields that the spaceport overlooks are filled with flowers of every color of the rainbow, and a sweet smell rests in the air. You end up finding James in one of the spaceport's gardens, and he waves you over to a table with a woman who is finishing off a steak. On the far side of the table is a map covered in annotations. As you get closer, the woman notices your arrival, wipes her mouth, and offers her hand."
msgstr "{1}の世界は花盛りです。宇宙港から見下ろす野原は虹のあらゆる色の花で埋め尽くされ、甘い香りが空気に漂っています。あなたは宇宙港の庭園の一つでジェームズを見つけます。彼はステーキを食べ終えようとしている女性が座るテーブルへ、あなたを手招きします。テーブルの向こう側には注釈が書き込まれた地図が広がっています。あなたが近づくと、女性はあなたの到着に気づき、口元を拭いて手を差し出します。"

#. [ES10-0261] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:347
msgctxt "ES10-0261"
msgid "{1}\"{2}, this is Captain Hwang,\" James says as you shake her hand. \"Rather than throwing you into the deep end of space combat, I figure you should try your hand at something a little safer. Hwang mines asteroids in this part of space and says there's a good system nearby if you're willing to give it a try.\""
msgstr "{1}「{2}、こちらはファン船長です」と、あなたが握手を交わす間、ジェームズが言います。「いきなり宇宙戦闘に放り込むより、もう少し安全なことに挑戦してみるのがいいと思います。ファン船長はこの宙域で小惑星採掘をしていて、試してみたいなら近くにいい星系があると言っていますよ」"

#. [ES10-0262] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:351
msgctxt "ES10-0262"
msgid "{1}\"Mining sounds interesting. I'll give it a shot.\""
msgstr "{1}「採掘というのは面白そうですね。やってみます」"

#. [ES10-0263] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:352
msgctxt "ES10-0263"
msgid "{1}\"I think I'm ready to head out on my own.\""
msgstr "{1}「そろそろ一人で出発する準備ができたと思います」"

#. [ES10-0264] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <captain> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:354
msgctxt "ES10-0264"
msgid "{1}\"That's good to hear,\" Captain {2} says with a smile. \"But be warned that mining isn't as easy as one might think. Especially without an asteroid scanner, mining can be just as much a test of your piloting skills as combat."
msgstr "{1}「それはいいですね」と{2}船長は微笑んで言います。「しかし、採掘は人が思うほど簡単ではないと忠告しておきます。特に小惑星スキャナーなしでは、採掘も戦闘と同じくらい操縦技術が試されることになるでしょう。"

#. [ES10-0265] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <they> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:355
msgctxt "ES10-0265"
msgid "{1}\"The first challenge,\" {2} continues, \"will be finding which asteroids are valuable. The worthless asteroids are either brown and smooth or gray and spiky with no apparent orbit. It doesn't matter how long you shoot them, they won't be destroyed. Valuable asteroids will always orbit the star and have a range of colors and surface textures. If you're not sure which are which and you don't have an asteroid scanner to tell you, keep a look out for other miners to see what they're firing at."
msgstr "{1}「最初の難関は」と{2}は続けます。「どの小惑星に価値があるかを見極めることです。価値のない小惑星は、茶色で滑らかか、あるいは灰色でトゲトゲしており、明確な軌道を持っていません。どれだけ長く撃ち続けても、破壊されることはありません。価値のある小惑星は常に恒星の周りを公転しており、さまざまな色や表面の質感を持っています。どれがどれだか分からず、見分けるための小惑星スキャナーも持っていない場合は、他の採掘者が何を撃っているかを見て参考にしてください。"

#. [ES10-0266] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:356
msgctxt "ES10-0266"
msgid "{1}\"Generally speaking, the more valuable minerals are tougher to mine, either because they're harder to break apart, or they're less common and in more dangerous regions of the galaxy. Silicon breaks up quickly; you'll fill your hold in a hurry and the stuff is everywhere. Platinum or gold asteroids are more work; they're not as common in areas where the Navy watches your back, but you make several times the number of credits for the effort."
msgstr "{1}「一般的に言って、より価値の高い鉱物ほど採掘は困難です。砕くのが難しいか、あるいは希少で銀河のより危険な地域にあるかのどちらかです。シリコンはすぐに砕けるので、すぐに貨物倉がいっぱいになりますし、どこにでもあります。プラチナや金の小惑星は手間がかかります。海軍が守ってくれるような地域ではあまり見かけませんが、その分、得られるクレジットは何倍にもなります」"

#. [ES10-0267] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:357
msgctxt "ES10-0267"
msgid "{1}\"I could go on, but I think you get the picture.\""
msgstr "{1}「まだ続けられますが、大体お分かりいただけたでしょう」"

#. [ES10-0268] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <captain>; <they>; <system> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:363
msgctxt "ES10-0268"
msgid "{1}You and James chat with {2} a while longer, and {3} suggests trying your hand at mining in {4}. \"It's a great place. You could throw a dart in that system and half the time you'd hit an asteroid worth at least something, and I've never been bothered by pirates while I've been there. The easiest asteroids to get there are the silicon ones; you can spot them by their slightly-green tint.\""
msgstr "{1}あなたとジェームズは{2}と少しの間談笑し、{3}は{4}で採掘に挑戦してみることを提案します。「あそこは素晴らしい場所ですよ。あの星系でダーツを投げれば、半分くらいの確率で何らかの価値がある小惑星に当たるでしょうし、私がそこにいた間、海賊に悩まされたことは一度もありません。あそこで一番採掘しやすいのはシリコンの小惑星です。少し緑がかった色をしているので見分けられますよ」"

#. [ES10-0269] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first>; <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:364
msgctxt "ES10-0269"
msgid "{1}\"That does sound like a good place for a beginner pilot,\" James says. \"How about we start small, {2}? Let's go mine at least five tons of silicon before landing on {3} and we can call it a day.\""
msgstr "{1}「確かに初心者パイロットには良い場所ですね」とジェームズは言う。「{2}、手始めに少しやってみませんか？少なくとも5トンのシリコンを採掘してから{3}に着陸して、今日は終わりにしましょう」"

#. [ES10-0270] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <system> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:368
msgctxt "ES10-0270"
msgid "{1}You and James chat with Hwang a while longer, and she suggests trying your hand at mining in {2}. \"It's a great place. You could throw a dart in that system and half the time you'd hit an asteroid worth at least something, and I've never been bothered by pirates while I've been there. The easiest asteroids to get there are the lead ones; you can spot them by their light gray, rounded appearance.\""
msgstr "{1}あなたとジェームズはファンともうしばらく話し、彼女は{2}で採掘に挑戦してみることを提案します。「素晴らしい場所ですよ。あの星系でダーツを投げれば、半分くらいの確率で何らかの価値がある小惑星に当たるでしょうし、私がそこにいた間、海賊に悩まされたことは一度もありません。そこで一番採掘しやすいのは鉛の小惑星です。薄い灰色で丸みを帯びた姿をしているので見分けられます」"

#. [ES10-0271] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first>; <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:369
msgctxt "ES10-0271"
msgid "{1}\"That does sound like a good place for a beginner pilot,\" James says. \"How about we start small, {2}? Let's go mine at least five tons of lead before landing on {3} and we can call it a day.\""
msgstr "{1}「確かに初心者パイロットには良い場所ですね」とジェームズは言う。「{2}、手始めに少しやってみませんか？少なくとも5トンの鉛を採掘してから{3}に着陸して、今日は終わりにしましょう」"

#. [ES10-0272] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:373
msgctxt "ES10-0272"
msgid "{1}You and James chat with August a while longer, and he suggests trying your hand at mining in Procyon. \"It's a great place. You could throw a dart in that system and half the time you'd hit an asteroid worth at least something, and I've never been bothered by pirates while I've been there. Just watch out for getting stranded; the only landable planet in Procyon is Cassandra, which is uninhabited. Still, merchant and Navy ships should come frequently enough that you can just hail one of them for a refuel.\""
msgstr "{1}あなたとジェームズはオーガストともうしばらく話し、彼はプロキオンで採掘に挑戦してみることを提案します。「素晴らしい場所ですよ。あの星系でダーツを投げれば、半分くらいの確率で何らかの価値がある小惑星に当たるでしょうし、私がそこにいた間、海賊に悩まされたことは一度もありません。ただ、立ち往生しないように気をつけてください。プロキオンで着陸可能な惑星はカサンドラだけで、そこは無人です。それでも、商船や海軍の船が頻繁に来るはずなので、そのうちの1隻に燃料補給を頼めばいいでしょう」"

#. [ES10-0273] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <first>; <system>; <planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:374
msgctxt "ES10-0273"
msgid "{1}\"That does sound like a good place for a beginner pilot,\" James says. \"How about we start small, {2}? Let's go mine at least five tons of silicon in Procyon before jumping to {3} and landing on {4}.\""
msgstr "{1}「確かに初心者パイロットには良い場所ですね」とジェームズは言う。「{2}、手始めに少しやってみませんか？プロキオンで少なくとも5トンのシリコンを採掘してから{3}へジャンプし、{4}に着陸しましょう」"

#. [ES10-0274] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:379
msgctxt "ES10-0274"
msgid "Once you've landed, you meet up with James and he asks you, \"What did you think of mining?\""
msgstr "着陸後、あなたがジェームズと合流すると、彼は「採掘はどうでしたか？」と尋ねる。"

#. [ES10-0275] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:381
msgctxt "ES10-0275"
msgid "{1}\"I can't believe anyone would do that much work.\""
msgstr "{1}「これほど大変な作業をする人がいるなんて信じられません」"

#. [ES10-0276] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:382
msgctxt "ES10-0276"
msgid "{1}\"That was great!\""
msgstr "{1}「最高でした！」"

#. [ES10-0277] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:383
msgctxt "ES10-0277"
msgid "{1}James nods and says, \"Chasing asteroids can be a challenge, but when you're starting off, mining can be a fast way to build cash for your next ship. It's also a great way to explore the galaxy. Jobs always follow the trade routes and settled areas. Mining makes it profitable to explore the nooks and crannies of the hyperlanes. If the place you end up landing has an economy, they'll buy the minerals in your hold. Mainly though, it's about how you like to spend your time. Some captains like managing a trading fleet while others like to strike out on their own."
msgstr "{1}ジェームズは頷いて言う。「小惑星を追いかけるのは大変かもしれませんが、始めたばかりの頃は、採掘は次の船のための資金を稼ぐ手っ取り早い方法になり得ます。銀河を探索するのにも最適な方法です。仕事は常に交易路や居住地域に沿って発生します。採掘をすれば、ハイパーレーンの隅々まで探索することが利益につながります。着陸先に経済活動があれば、貨物倉にある鉱物を買い取ってもらえるでしょう。ですが、結局のところは、あなたがどのように時間を使いたいかによります。貿易船団を管理するのが好きな船長もいれば、独力で道を切り開くのが好きな船長もいますから」"

#. [ES10-0278] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:384
msgctxt "ES10-0278"
msgid "{1}\"Mining can be complex compared to running jobs or trading commodities. I learned that first hand after pirates disabled my ship when I was starting out and I worked aboard a mining ship while it was being repaired. Now that was a while back so I might be a little rusty, but I could try at answering any other questions you might have about mining.\""
msgstr "{1}「採掘は、仕事の請負や商品の取引と比べると複雑な場合があります。私が駆け出しの頃、海賊に船を無力化され、その修理中に採掘船で働いて身をもって知りました。もう随分前のことなので少し勘が鈍っているかもしれませんが、採掘について他に質問があれば、答えてみますよ」"

#. [ES10-0279] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:388
msgctxt "ES10-0279"
msgid "{1}\"What equipment do I need to mine?\""
msgstr "{1}「採掘にはどんな装備が必要ですか？」"

#. [ES10-0280] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:391
msgctxt "ES10-0280"
msgid "{1}\"How do you deal with pirates?\""
msgstr "{1}「海賊にはどう対処するのですか？」"

#. [ES10-0281] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. Conditional text; inspect attached display/activation condition. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:395
msgctxt "ES10-0281"
msgid "{1}\"How can I check the value of minerals?\""
msgstr "{1}「鉱物の価値はどうやって確認できますか？」"

#. [ES10-0282] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:399
msgctxt "ES10-0282"
msgid "{1}\"I think I have enough information.\""
msgstr "{1}「もう十分な情報が得られたと思います」"

#. [ES10-0283] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:404
msgctxt "ES10-0283"
msgid "{1}\"Well, you need a weapon that does hull damage,\" James says. \"A Beam Laser will get the job done, but it will take a while. If you want to optimize your mining operations, however, you'll want a Mining Laser. Not only does it cut through asteroids faster, it's also more precise and preserves more minerals when the asteroid breaks apart. Some miners like to have a bit of combat flexibility by mining with Heavy Lasers, however."
msgstr "{1}「そうですね、船体にダメージを与える武器が必要です」とジェームズは言う。「ビームレーザーでも用は足りますが、時間がかかります。しかし、採掘作業を最適化したいなら、採掘レーザーが欲しくなるでしょう。小惑星をより速く切り崩せるだけでなく、より正確で、小惑星が砕けた時に鉱物をより多く残せます。ただ、重レーザーで採掘して戦闘の柔軟性を少し持たせたいという採掘者もいますね」"

#. [ES10-0284] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:405
msgctxt "ES10-0284"
msgid "{1}\"Aside from lasers, the most valuable tool is an asteroid scanner. They're expensive, but they connect into your navigation and targeting systems to point you towards minable asteroids. You can also set them to find the most valuable asteroids, which increases your profitability per run. After that, a tactical scanner will tell you how far away the asteroid is and show how much damage you're doing. An afterburner is good for chasing down fast moving asteroids or getting away from pirates without leaving the system. A ramscoop will let you refuel while mining, extend your exploration range, and allow you to be ready for a quick escape.\""
msgstr "{1}「レーザー以外で最も役立つツールは小惑星スキャナーです。高価ですが、航法システムや照準システムと連動して、採掘可能な小惑星の位置を教えてくれます。価値の高い小惑星を優先して探すよう設定することもでき、1回の採掘で得られる利益が増えます。その次に役立つ戦術スキャナーは、小惑星までの距離と、小惑星に与えているダメージを表示してくれます。アフターバーナーは、高速で移動する小惑星を追いかけたり、星系を離れずに海賊から逃げたりするのに役立ちます。ラムスクープがあれば、採掘中に燃料を補給でき、探索範囲を広げられるうえ、すぐに脱出できるよう備えられます」"

#. [ES10-0285] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:407
msgctxt "ES10-0285"
msgid "{1}\"I can't fit all that on my ship!\""
msgstr "{1}「そんなにたくさん、自分の船には装備できませんよ！」"

#. [ES10-0286] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:409
msgctxt "ES10-0286"
msgid "{1}\"That all makes sense.\""
msgstr "{1}「なるほど、よく分かりました」"

#. [ES10-0287] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:410
msgctxt "ES10-0287"
msgid "{1}\"Anything else you want to ask me?\" says James."
msgstr "{1}「他に何か聞きたいことはありますか？」とジェームズは言う。"

#. [ES10-0288] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <model> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:413
msgctxt "ES10-0288"
msgid "{1}James gives you a knowing smile as he answers, \"Not in a factory build, you won't. But you'd be surprised how much space you can free up even in a {2} if you're willing to be flexible. Do you really need that much power? If you've got an outfitter on the planet where you're mining, do you need a hyperdrive, or even a shield generator? Maybe a cargo expansion would be of more use.\" He pauses briefly, perhaps considering what liability he's opened himself up for, then adds, \"I'm not saying you should, of course, but you have options.\""
msgstr "{1}ジェームズは訳知り顔で微笑んで答える。「工場出荷時の構成では無理でしょうね。ですが、装備を柔軟に見直す気があれば、{2}でも驚くほどスペースを空けられますよ。本当にそれほどの電力が必要ですか？採掘先の惑星に装備屋があるなら、ハイパードライブや、そもそもシールドジェネレーターは必要でしょうか？貨物室を拡張した方が役に立つかもしれません」彼は少し言葉を止める。自分がどんな責任を負うことになるか考えたのかもしれない。そして付け加える。「もちろん、そうすべきだと言っているわけではありません。ただ、選択肢はあるということです」"

#. [ES10-0289] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:419
msgctxt "ES10-0289"
msgid "{1}\"You can always bribe them to leave you alone. If the minerals are good enough and you have enough cargo capacity, you'll still turn a profit. Or if you have a fast ship, you can just run away. Of course, with enough of a fleet you just fight them off.\" He shakes his head. \"Most pirates would be richer and live longer if they just mined instead of extorting merchants and plundering ships.\""
msgstr "{1}「賄賂を渡して見逃してもらうこともできます。鉱物の価値が十分に高く、貨物の積載量も足りていれば、それでも利益は出ます。あるいは、船が速ければ逃げるだけでもいい。もちろん、十分な規模の艦隊があれば撃退できます」彼は首を振る。「ほとんどの海賊は、商人を脅して金を取ったり船を略奪したりするより、自分で採掘した方が裕福になれるし、長生きもできるでしょうに」"

#. [ES10-0290] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:425
msgctxt "ES10-0290"
msgid "{1}\"You will learn this by experience, but if the planet has an outfitter, you can check the price there before you sell.\""
msgstr "{1}「そのうち経験で分かるようになりますが、惑星に装備屋があれば、売る前にそこで価格を確認できます」"

#. [ES10-0291] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:435
msgctxt "ES10-0291"
msgid "{1}\"If you're willing to take me on one more journey,\" James says, \"meet me in the spaceport bar in a little while. Don't forget to sell off your minerals at the trading post, or if there is one, the outfitter.\""
msgstr "{1}「もう一度私を連れて行ってくれるなら」とジェームズは言う。「少ししたら宇宙港のバーで会いましょう。鉱物は忘れずに交易所か、装備屋があればそこで売っておいてください」"

#. [ES10-0292] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro end" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:438
msgctxt "ES10-0292"
msgid "{1}\"If you'd rather whet your teeth with some starfighting, come and find me in the spaceport before you leave.\" He picks up his suitcase and heads outside."
msgstr "{1}「宇宙戦で腕試しがしたいなら、出発前に宇宙港で私を訪ねてくれ」彼はスーツケースを手に取ると、外へと向かった。"

#. [ES10-0294] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:444
msgctxt "ES10-0294"
msgid "You find James sitting at the spaceport's tiny bar, sipping a beer while watching the large displays that show the landing pads and the irrigated fields beyond. The displays are supposed to make the underground building feel less claustrophobic."
msgstr "ジェームズが宇宙港の小さなバーに座り、ビールを飲みながら、着陸パッドとその向こうに広がる灌漑農地を映し出す大型ディスプレイを眺めているのが見える。そのディスプレイは、地下の建物が醸し出す閉塞感を和らげるためのものだ。"

#. [ES10-0295] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:445
msgctxt "ES10-0295"
msgid "{1}\"This is one of the least habitable planets in the galaxy. But if it doesn't kill us instantly, then someone's tried to settle it.\" He pauses for a moment while gazing at one of the displays. You spot a sandstorm picking up in the far distance as the workers in the fields hastily finish their work before it arrives."
msgstr "{1}「ここは銀河系で最も居住に適さない惑星の一つだ。だが、もし即座に死ぬような場所でなければ、誰かが入植を試みているはずだ」彼はディスプレイの一つを見つめながら、一瞬言葉を切る。遠くで砂嵐が巻き起こるのが見え、畑の作業員たちがそれが到着する前に慌ただしく仕事を終えようとしている。"

#. [ES10-0296] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:446
msgctxt "ES10-0296"
msgid "{1}\"Care for a drink?\" he asks."
msgstr "{1}「何か飲むか？」と彼は尋ねる。"

#. [ES10-0297] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:448
msgctxt "ES10-0297"
msgid "{1}\"Sure.\""
msgstr "{1}「ああ、もらおう」"

#. [ES10-0298] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:449
msgctxt "ES10-0298"
msgid "{1}\"No thanks.\""
msgstr "{1}「いや、遠慮しておく」"

#. [ES10-0299] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <home planet> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:451
msgctxt "ES10-0299"
msgid "{1}He buys you a beer. It tastes a little stale, but it's not the worst beer you've ever had. You can't help but feel sorry for the people who work here, so isolated and cut off from even the basic amenities you took for granted on {2}."
msgstr "{1}彼があなたにビールを奢ってくれる。少し気が抜けているが、これまでに飲んだ中で最悪というわけではない。ここで働く人々に同情せずにはいられない。彼らはあまりに孤立しており、あなたが{2}で当たり前だと思っていた基本的な生活環境さえも奪われているのだから。"

#. [ES10-0300] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:453
msgctxt "ES10-0300"
msgid "{1}\"Anyway,\" says James, \"would you be willing to take me on one more journey? It's time for me to head for that retirement home.\""
msgstr "{1}「とにかく」とジェームズは言う。「もう一度だけ私を旅に連れて行ってくれないか？そろそろあの老人ホームへ向かう時間なんだ」"

#. [ES10-0302] Scope: Core | Category: James tutorial | Source context: conversation "mining intro new sahara" | Text role: choice | Route / branch: Interceptor (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Contains literal paragraph-indentation tab. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:456
msgctxt "ES10-0302"
msgid "{1}\"Sorry, I think I'll go hunt some pirates instead.\""
msgstr "{1}「ごめん、やっぱり海賊狩りに行くことにするよ」"

#. [ES10-0304] Scope: Optional | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [0 Fighter] | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Invalid starter purchase (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Localization notes: Preserve substitution tokens exactly; translate template before substitution. (annotates: general; from: developer)
#. Tokens to preserve: <flagship model> (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:495
msgctxt "ES10-0304"
msgid "As you check over the specs of your brand new {1} one last time, you realize it lacks the hyperdrive necessary for interstellar travel! Unless you're happy to spend the rest of your life flying past the same few planets, you'll need to sell the {2} and buy a proper spacefaring vessel."
msgstr "新品の{1}の仕様を最後にもう一度確認していると、恒星間航行に必要なハイパードライブが搭載されていないことに気づく！残りの人生を同じいくつかの惑星のそばを飛び続けて過ごすのが嫌なら、その{2}を売って、まともな宇宙船を買い直す必要がある。"

#. [ES10-0305] Scope: Optional | Category: James tutorial | Source context: Intro [0 Drone] | Text role: dialogue paragraph | Route / branch: Invalid starter purchase (annotates: general; from: developer)
#: data/human/intro missions.txt:509
msgctxt "ES10-0305"
msgid "You prepare to board your new ship and take it for a test flight, only to find it is an automated drone that lacks a crew compartment entirely! Unless you want to try strapping yourself on the outside of the hull, you'll need to sell off your drone and buy a proper spacefaring vessel."
msgstr "新しい船に乗り込み、試験飛行に出ようとした矢先、それが乗組員用の区画が全くない自動ドローンであることに気づく！船体の外側に自分を縛り付けるつもりがないのなら、そのドローンを売却して、まともな宇宙船を買い直す必要がある。"

